No objections; however, there is another consistency to consider:
vmlinuz (if I remember correctly) is a self-unpacking kernel image,
while alpha's vmlinux.gz is a normal gzipped file.  Even if MILO looks
at the magic number, people still prefer file name suffices.  Knowing
that, say, vmlinux-VERSION.gz is a real gzipped file may potentially be
helpful.  That is, there is actually a choice which consistency to break.

